The early return when the framework is not `@storybook/react-vite` is completely silent. A user running `storybook ai init` on an Angular, Vue, or Svelte project will see zero output and have no way to understand why nothing happened. The same no-op occurs in agent mode (via `initiate.ts`), where the caller also receives no feedback.

At minimum, emit a message before returning:
```ts
logger.warn(
  `The 'storybook ai init' command currently only supports @storybook/react-vite projects. Detected framework: ${projectInfo.framework}`
);
return;
```
The limitation should also appear in the CLI help text for `storybook ai init`.
